// The Supported mods tab (SupportedModList). Status: Works, Settings (works with Settings sync on), Partial or Broken.
// details: what works; setup: what the host must turn on or avoid; limits: what does not work. One plain sentence each. Update this when a release changes what a mod gets.
{
  "general": [
    "Settings sync: the host's MCM settings reach every joining player, and live changes are sent at once. Players install ModderLords.Compat, which the launcher keeps up to date.",
    "Locked to host: per mod, choose whether players get the server's settings or keep their own (Mods tab).",
    "Roles: each mod can be Server, Client, Client-optional or Dependency-only, and single folders can be kept off the server, so art and UI stay off the headless server.",
    "Load order: dependencies are respected and Coop's position is shown. Mods that must load after Coop are moved for you, or Fix load order is offered.",
    "Map-replacing mods: the server prepares its own copy of the map and handles missing home towns. Field battles avoid scenes that would crash.",
    "Kingdom votes: votes of any mod's own types reach players, and players who do not vote in time are decided for by the AI.",
    "Quests and stashes: the game's \"inventory exchanged\" event fires in co-op, so delivery quests and mods that listen for it work.",
    "Server-only logic (experimental, Server tab, Advanced): a mod's campaign logic runs only on the host. Works for some mods only.",
    "Compatibility verdicts: the Mods tab shows Works, Needs recipe, Broken or Unknown for each mod, and you can submit your own findings."
  ],
